Yes, if {gonai} is defined as above, equivalence between {go ... gi ... gi=
=20
...} and {go nai ... gi nai ... gi nai ...} will be broken. We need to keep=
=20
{go ... gi ...} and {go nai ... gi nai ...} be equivalent in the case of=20
n=3D2. Would this change of meaning of {GA nai} hurt usefulness of binary=
=20
connective system? If we carefully define {GA (nai)} of n-ary connective=20
system, it might be possible to keep the binary connective system safe.

